atorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty ,$ we require $a>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334290/field-5" "q-334290/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" :answer/id #uuid "78a4984d-5107-53f2-8757-b68d38554681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e" :answer/id #uuid "1d7714b8-c8ee-5654-aab6-d759db1d0667" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1/0dbbee0924d29cddc95e729e19738a391c447170486ca6319bb5fb581d916120" :answer/id #uuid "9dadab2c-4679-50be-bb0a-3db2eafaf83a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1/ae17e2311ebdcb443976f856340f688b68e78591b3ccdd9c5d8ffe3ef1675120" :answer/id #uuid "e1aa188a-0a67-5cf4-bf71-2fef57657e7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" :answer/id #uuid "6299ab89-c27e-554f-8bab-c8c36030738a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1/590e223dd2b8bc7487dd03750c9d33f095cb4f45e3bb1a22990cb31f166d0d54" :answer/id #uuid "c17589e1-0a25-5fb9-ad40-df334687c76f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "78a75909-b3d2-5abf-8c2b-37fcd31f2c84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334317/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" :answer-field/choices ["q-334317/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" "q-334317/field-1/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e" "q-334317/field-1/0dbbee0924d29cddc95e729e19738a391c447170486ca6319bb5fb581d916120" "q-334317/field-1/ae17e2311ebdcb443976f856340f688b68e78591b3ccdd9c5d8ffe3ef1675120" "q-334317/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" "q-334317/field-1/590e223dd2b8bc7487dd03750c9d33f095cb4f45e3bb1a22990cb31f166d0d54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" :answer/id #uuid "4f4d7d2a-3645-5640-8f0b-48499353ee21" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-2/4912676f4da8ab51f553f74fb01abf9e1196a836c79544d0c8b6e6f56bf62370" :answer/id #uuid "16aa42d9-7e7d-58a8-ae97-fc673f73e732" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b" :answer/id #uuid "e1719ad0-e4e7-54c2-b39d-e4d534c93643" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a center" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bdb1dc1-1fad-5e1b-af72-4a76ee98cb45" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334317/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b" :answer-field/choices ["q-334317/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" "q-334317/field-2/4912676f4da8ab51f553f74fb01abf9e1196a836c79544d0c8b6e6f56bf62370" "q-334317/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334317" :question/id #uuid "a3170fb5-aeaf-54a0-a955-4e3e36f0bf2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-334317" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=8x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{0\\cdot t}=1$ for all $t.$ Thus, we have an ellipse that curves around the origin. \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a center}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334317/field-1" "q-334317/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" :answer/id #uuid "f180ddce-498c-5e3d-b9f9-ae4d6ecc7007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" :answer/id #uuid "ea500eee-587b-5259-ab81-8ff5cdfa3e04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1/ae17e2311ebdcb443976f856340f688b68e78591b3ccdd9c5d8ffe3ef1675120" :answer/id #uuid "d8d5b9fb-8bc8-5819-a55d-2ce20be58bc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1/590e223dd2b8bc7487dd03750c9d33f095cb4f45e3bb1a22990cb31f166d0d54" :answer/id #uuid "1e5e3f55-518b-5c85-bdf7-75f1b305bb48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1/0dbbee0924d29cddc95e729e19738a391c447170486ca6319bb5fb581d916120" :answer/id #uuid "0118303a-d35e-56f4-bb63-cb75f39494d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e" :answer/id #uuid "b88c5122-8a3f-56b7-b7bf-92be0241bbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "59aeef77-555b-5dde-8b58-4d92cde71096" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334313/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-334313/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" "q-334313/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" "q-334313/field-1/ae17e2311ebdcb443976f856340f688b68e78591b3ccdd9c5d8ffe3ef1675120" "q-334313/field-1/590e223dd2b8bc7487dd03750c9d33f095cb4f45e3bb1a22990cb31f166d0d54" "q-334313/field-1/0dbbee0924d29cddc95e729e19738a391c447170486ca6319bb5fb581d916120" "q-334313/field-1/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" :answer/id #uuid "e9121cca-e178-5717-bec0-3e02135dd32e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b" :answer/id #uuid "7cfd5d7d-7888-5f86-b5bc-82f2caa8056d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a center" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-2/4912676f4da8ab51f553f74fb01abf9e1196a836c79544d0c8b6e6f56bf62370" :answer/id #uuid "2d51ed88-8ad7-58ea-98c7-f218e4fda633" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfb132e3-d9ec-5824-8965-3f619f403e1e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334313/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" :answer-field/choices ["q-334313/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" "q-334313/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b" "q-334313/field-2/4912676f4da8ab51f553f74fb01abf9e1196a836c79544d0c8b6e6f56bf62370"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334313" :question/id #uuid "03dd338f-f62c-5a74-8bc2-3f64ac3029db" :question/math-academy-id "q-334313" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=-1<0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable spiral (sink)}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334313/field-1" "q-334313/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334313"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1/ae17e2311ebdcb443976f856340f688b68e78591b3ccdd9c5d8ffe3ef1675120" :answer/id #uuid "a5ac33cd-cfd6-5214-ad8e-54ea8a17f2f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1/590e223dd2b8bc7487dd03750c9d33f095cb4f45e3bb1a22990cb31f166d0d54" :answer/id #uuid "eeec1ef7-47ff-5236-9d8c-098957265ebe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1/0dbbee0924d29cddc95e729e19738a391c447170486ca6319bb5fb581d916120" :answer/id #uuid "37f44135-fadb-555e-8064-a7b47ebe8c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" :answer/id #uuid "ffe7bb18-a566-560c-90d4-0ac057427a2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e" :answer/id #uuid "56a51e4f-e9a8-5de2-b28a-c2ef2a416946" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" :answer/id #uuid "0ef798a7-5611-5d03-911f-288300169c6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "904ce9a5-6b52-5ee3-b4cd-58f794926de3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334314/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a" :answer-field/choices ["q-334314/field-1/ae17e2311ebdcb443976f856340f688b68e78591b3ccdd9c5d8ffe3ef1675120" "q-334314/field-1/590e223dd2b8bc7487dd03750c9d33f095cb4f45e3bb1a22990cb31f166d0d54" "q-334314/field-1/0dbbee0924d29cddc95e729e19738a391c447170486ca6319bb5fb581d916120" "q-334314/field-1/5f8e96fcef1cbe01e6835a0848fdcdb5b4ddc544a7a4da93a09510fb4372f8f7" "q-334314/field-1/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e" "q-334314/field-1/3eedad2b68f9e406204290c223fc7f33368e09cf74b8e7e09666a6fecaf84e6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-2/4912676f4da8ab51f553f74fb01abf9e1196a836c79544d0c8b6e6f56bf62370" :answer/id #uuid "2a571d37-2311-58c5-9036-77eb84cd562d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" :answer/id #uuid "28d396a5-b727-5937-853c-34b715f732d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b" :answer/id #uuid "f79c1086-2062-5394-8e19-d4e059ee3811" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a center" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "54d3717b-e60d-52dc-92fd-8e29b7e3c0bb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334314/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b" :answer-field/choices ["q-334314/field-2/4912676f4da8ab51f553f74fb01abf9e1196a836c79544d0c8b6e6f56bf62370" "q-334314/field-2/0567ded365958d2b96c61c7991783dbda12d049410d79502fa82922588990c17" "q-334314/field-2/280edb51317f6a9c5b7147d2a4082131cdd45ac1307ffcecbd6e4226c2d1682b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334314" :question/id #uuid "a5375147-d196-584f-972b-e134511044e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-334314" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{0\\cdot t}=1$ for all $t.$ Thus, we have an ellipse that curves around the origin. \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a center}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334314/field-1" "q-334314/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334314"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186167181 :question/answer-fields 17592186164499] {:db/id "q-334307/field-1/ma-v1/18e9b39a3a504d305bc6cd887976b1281c24aade77a4129d5b3b8c7a60f76e1a/47660004af8c7eb8cb3de5f83042d3129092485a315696ee6f14551021a20f8e" :answer/id #uuid "f286b861-9641-577b-8d6c-f3e474bfb852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/ensure [:answe